From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usbscan.sys: the USB scanner driver

Our own implementation of the USB still image driver over wineusb.sys, with
the still image class's shared INF (sti.inf, in %windir%\inf): a device INF's
"Needs=STI.USBSection.Services" adds it. Programs open \\.\UsbscanN (or
\\.\UsbscanN\<pipe>): ReadFile/WriteFile go to the bulk pipes, and the
usbscan.h IOCTLs give the device descriptor and pipes, vendor and class
control requests (IOCTL_READ/WRITE_REGISTERS, IOCTL_SEND_USB_REQUEST), the
interrupt pipe's events, cancel and reset. Bulk and interrupt transfers
complete asynchronously. IOCTL_WRITE_REGISTERS reports the bytes written,
as the Ambir ImageScan Pro 490i's library checks.
---
